# .gitignore — from 00-README §7.2.
#
# Read the OTHER direction first. This file decides what can never be committed
# and — far more dangerously — what can never be LOST. Six of the paths a fresh
# clone must carry look exactly like build output:
#
#   pubspec.lock · drift_schemas/drift_schema_v<N>.json ·
#   lib/l10n/app_localizations*.dart · test/drift/generated/** ·
#   test/features/goldens/*.png · test/fixtures/*.json
#
# `drift_schemas/` is the one 00-README §7.1 calls UNRECOVERABLE: it is the
# migration tests' only baseline and there is no server-side copy of anybody's
# phone. An ignore line for any directory named `generated` reads as tidy and
# silently drops test/drift/generated; `*localizations*` drops the committed
# gen-l10n output; a bare `*.json` drops drift_schemas AND test/fixtures. Every
# one of those is invisible until somebody clones the repository months later.
#
# test/policy/tree_shape_test.dart asserts BOTH directions with
# `git check-ignore`, which answers for every .gitignore in the repository
# rather than for this one file. This is the file in this epic that is never
# waved through.

# ── The seven from 00-README §7.2 ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Every comment here is on its OWN line, and that is not a style choice. In a
# .gitignore a `#` starts a comment only at the START of a line — a trailing
# one is part of the pattern, so `.fvm/    # the SDK cache` is a rule that
# matches nothing and ignores nothing, silently. The first draft of this file
# had five such lines and `git check-ignore` in tree_shape_test.dart caught all
# five.

# The FVM SDK cache. `.fvmrc` is COMMITTED — one character apart, and the
# failure is silent in both directions: ignore `.fvmrc` and CI's toolchain-pin
# assert has nothing to read; commit `.fvm/` and you have added a Flutter SDK
# to the repository.
.fvm/
.dart_tool/
/build/
# lcov.info is a CI artefact, never a committed file.
/coverage/
# Local only; regenerate from the keystore and its passwords.
android/key.properties
# The upload keystore itself.
android/*.jks
android/*.keystore
# Obfuscation symbols — kept forever OFF the laptop, never in git.
symbols-archive/

# ── Editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
.atom/
.build/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.swiftpm/
migrate_working_dir/
# The .vscode folder holds launch configurations somebody may want committed.
#.vscode/

# ── Flutter / Dart build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release

# ── Obfuscation and symbolication ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Losing an obfuscation symbols directory makes every stack trace in every
# diagnostics log a user ever sends for that build permanently unreadable. The
# symbols are git-ignored above AND kept off the laptop under
# symbols-archive/<name>+<build>/ — the ignore line exists so nobody solves the
# second half by committing them.
app.*.symbols
app.*.map.json

# G1's three working files (`tool/assert_permissions.sh`). Written into the
# repository root because the script is run from there, both on CI and by hand.
# Anchored with a leading solidus so each matches at the root and nowhere else —
# an unanchored `merged-manifest.xml` would also hide one somebody deliberately
# committed as a fixture.
/merged-manifest.xml
/actual-permissions.txt
/expected-sorted.txt

# **GOLDEN FAILURE OUTPUT, WHICH IS A CI ARTEFACT AND NEVER A COMMIT**
# (`12 §8.4` rule 5). `matchesGoldenFile` writes `<name>_testImage.png`,
# `_masterImage.png` and `_isolatedDiff.png` here on a mismatch, and the
# tempting mistake is committing one as "the new baseline" — it is a rendering
# of the failure, not of the screen. Re-baselining is `make goldens-update`,
# alone, in its own commit.
test/features/failures/

# Workflow worktrees — transient, and each is a git repo of its own.
.claude/worktrees/
